{
  "id": "mcdonald-s-happy-meal",
  "name": "McDonald's Happy Meal",
  "category": "retailer_promotion",
  "description": {
    "text": "McDonald's restaurants in Japan gave out Pokémon cards with their Happy Meals (Happy Sets) in eight campaigns from 2002 to 2007, most of them early in the year: one card with each meal, which card a surprise. Each campaign had its own five to ten cards with Pokémon of the moment: e-Card era alternate-art cards in 2002, the Hoenn starters and their final forms with Latias, Latios, Plusle and Minun for the ADV era in 2003 and 2004, cards of the 2005 film Lucario and the Mystery of Mew that July, and Pokémon new to Diamond & Pearl in 2007. Many of the 2005 and 2006 drawings were also used on English cards, in EX sets and the POP Series packs.\n\nOutside Japan, Pokémon has run a Happy Meal card promotion with McDonald's most years since 2011. It began in North America and went on to other countries, Europe and Canada among them, and each year's cards are a set of their own. In 2013 they came only in France and in 2016 only in Europe, and in 2018 and 2019 France had a larger set of its own. Since 2021 each Happy Meal has held a pack of four cards.",
